Short:        Smart File System handler for 68020+
Author:       Ilkka Lehtoranta
Uploader:     ilkleht gmail com (Ilkka Lehtoranta)
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Requires:     AmigaOS 2.04+, 68020+, existing SFS0 volume
URL:          https://github.com/ilehtoranta/CopperSFS
Distribution: Aminet

CopperSFS 1.0 is an experimental AmigaDOS filesystem handler for classic
Smart File System (SFS\0) volumes. It is an independent implementation of
the filesystem originally developed by John Hendrikx.

The package contains one 68020+ filesystem handler, the CopperSFSCtrl
command and documentation. Install CopperSFS as L:CopperSFS on a separate
boot volume, and CopperSFSCtrl in C:.

Use disposable test volumes with independent backups. Physical devices and
other ROM configurations remain unqualified. Device access beyond 4 GiB
requires TD64. NSD is not supported; native large-device use remains
unqualified.

The default is buffered writes with a 256 KiB clean-data cache. Configure
each mounted volume without replacing the handler:
  CopperSFSCtrl SFS0: INFO
  CopperSFSCtrl SFS0: DATACACHE 128K
  CopperSFSCtrl SFS0: DATACACHE OFF
  CopperSFSCtrl SFS0: WRITEMODE STRICT
  CopperSFSCtrl SFS0: WRITEMODE BUFFERED
  CopperSFSCtrl SFS0: FLUSH

Settings last for the mount. Boot-time preferences can be applied from
S:User-Startup after mounting. Cache changes preserve open handles and
pending writes. Mode changes checkpoint first; a failed change leaves the
previous mode active. FLUSH checks filesystem checkpoint success.

Recent unflushed buffered changes may be lost after a crash. Strict mode
commits each successful mutation before replying. Both use the same
recovery journal and ordered flush barriers. Recover interrupted CSUN
transactions with CopperSFS before using another filesystem handler.

The default loaded-and-mounted memory measured 585,480 bytes in the test
profile. INFO shows actual allocations; INSTALL.txt explains cache sizes,
allocation failures, startup settings and durability.

Comparison testing uses 68k SmartFilesystem 1.279 from Joerg Strohmayer's
development branch under Kickstart 3.1. See VALIDATION.txt and RELEASE.json
for the exact qualified hashes, recovery coverage and crash-model limits.

Read INSTALL.txt before installation. Verify files against SHA256SUMS.txt
on a host with SHA-256 support. CopperSFS uses the MIT license in LICENSE.txt.
Native handler integration source is not included.

Report reproducible problems at the public repository, including handler
hash, CPU, OS, device, geometry and steps using a disposable volume.
